nodecode-jet-browser is a rewrite of masakaai's masakaai/jet-browser:
https://github.com/masakaai/jet-browser
commit 1b0b10feb70e52bde844ba4e1cb7c35600af4b35
Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Jet Browser contributors (LICENSE)

The original is an integration for another agent harness: `integrations/hermes`,
one Python module that registers a single tool and, when the tool is called,
starts the project's digest-pinned Jet Browser image with Docker, drives its
ordered JSONL protocol (create, navigate, snapshot, input, evaluate,
screenshot, close), checks the evidence, and removes the container.

This rewrite keeps that one bounded operation and its protocol, in Common Lisp:
the same tool under the same name and with the same JSON evidence, the same
fixed `docker run` argument vector, the same pinned image and the same
checked-in seccomp profile, carried over unchanged into this folder. What it
adds is Nodecode's own surface — a declared config section the setup panel and
the model's primer both read, a `/jetbrowser` command, a manual topic, and an
option to keep the captured PNG — and what it leaves out is the Hermes plugin
API itself: there is no other harness here to register with. The original's
Python unit tests are replaced by this folder's Common Lisp tests, which run
the cell against a scripted container and need no Docker.
